<title>USA: America First stake cut by Cramer group.</title>
<headline>America First stake cut by Cramer group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investor James Cramer said Wednesday it cut its stake in America First Financial Fund to 390,000 benefical unit certificates, or 6.5 percent, from 7.8 percent previously.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 67,300 certificates sold between December 2 and January 23 at prices ranging from $28.75 to $30.25 per certificate.</p>
</text>
